WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:02.585
A colour analogue photograph,

00:02.919 --> 00:06.881
10.2 x 15.2 cm,

00:07.298 --> 00:08.842
horizontal format,

00:09.342 --> 00:10.427
depicts her smiling.

00:10.969 --> 00:23.523
I’m not sure who captured her, but I still own the point-and-shoot Charman AW-750 camera, a ’90s relic I keep as memorabilia.

00:24.190 --> 00:25.150
Her lips,

00:25.400 --> 00:27.235
slightly tinted blue,

00:27.610 --> 00:30.572
hint at where my anemia came from,

00:30.947 --> 00:37.954
and so do the two sweaters she’s wearing, despite what appears to be late spring;

00:38.288 --> 00:40.832
everyone else in the photo is wearing summer clothes.

00:41.541 --> 00:46.880
This is the only known photograph of her outside the apartment,

00:46.963 --> 00:52.761
before the police began knocking on doors and escorting people to the border.

00:53.344 --> 01:01.853
In all other photographs, taken later, she is sitting on her couch, either staring at the camera or chasing me.

01:02.228 --> 01:12.447
I am usually out of frame or blurred, unaware that, in the register of the nation-state, our roles have been swapped.

01:13.198 --> 01:15.658
Only, she is not blurred;

01:15.950 --> 01:17.994
she is invisible.
